{
  "title": "New Testament core: little words",
  "note": "The most frequent New Testament words are small ones: καί alone occurs about 9,000 times. Some, like δέ, γάρ and οὖν, are postpositive: they never come first in their clause (ὁ δὲ Ἰησοῦς, 'but Jesus'). οὐ negates statements of fact (indicative verbs); μή negates commands, wishes and conditions, and in the New Testament also participles.",
